WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:07.620
The last gasps of the Snyderverse, Battinson's&nbsp;
second outing, and the glorious return of the Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:13.664
of Steel. As DC turns to a new chapter, which of&nbsp;
these upcoming movies are you most excited to see?

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:19.140
For a moment, it really looked like Henry Cavill&nbsp;
was coming back for Man of Steel 2. After leaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:25.080
The Witcher and making a cameo appearance in Black&nbsp;
Adam, Cavill was all set to don the cape and get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:30.720
back to fighting crime. However, after James Gunn&nbsp;
and Peter Safran took over the newly named DCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:36.180
Man of Steel 2 was quickly scrapped and&nbsp;
Cavill was retired from the role of Superman.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:40.440
So what's in store for Superman&nbsp;
in the all-new DC Universe? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:45.660
Gunn and Safran announced their initial&nbsp;
slate of DCU projects on January 31st,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:50.220
2023, and the biggest film in&nbsp;
the works is Superman: Legacy.

00:00:50.419 --> 00:00:54.199
"Next up is the big one, the&nbsp;
true beginning of the DCU."

00:00:54.199 --> 00:00:58.860
Gunn wrote the film and Safran is hoping to&nbsp;
get him to direct — and it is, apparently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:02.220
not another superhero origin story. Safran said:

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:06.300
"It focuses on Superman balancing&nbsp;
his Kryptonian heritage with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:11.520
human upbringing. He is kindness in a world&nbsp;
that thinks of kindness as old-fashioned."

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:16.740
Casting remains unknown on Superman: Legacy, which&nbsp;
is scheduled to hit movie theaters on July 11th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:21.600
2025. We also know that it will kick&nbsp;
off the first chapter of the new DCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.465
which Gunn and Safran have given&nbsp;
the name "Gods &amp; Monsters."

00:01:25.465 --> 00:01:31.500
Warner Bros. and DC Comics know they've got one&nbsp;
of the most lucrative franchises of all time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:38.880
with Batman and his vast world of side characters,&nbsp;
villains, settings, and lore. To that end, Warner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:44.040
has multiple Batman-based movies in the works that&nbsp;
are pretty much entirely separate from each other.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:50.100
In addition to the Birds of Prey offshoot Black&nbsp;
Canary and Joker and its sequel, there's 2022's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:55.740
The Batman, starring Robert Pattinson as a nascent&nbsp;
Dark Knight. The cast, and co-writer-director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.740 --> 00:02:01.260
Matt Reeves, did such a good job establishing&nbsp;
this new Batman world that Warner Bros. grew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:07.200
keen on expanding it. The movie's $770 million&nbsp;
box office haul probably didn't hurt, either.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.300
The expansion of Reeves' Bat-verse will&nbsp;
begin with the HBO series The Penguin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:17.520
with Colin Farrell reprising his titular role.&nbsp;
Meanwhile, Reeves is actively conceptualizing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:22.200
The Batman Part II, which is set to be&nbsp;
released on October 3rd, 2025 — but it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:27.720
won't be part of the DCU proper. Instead, Part&nbsp;
II will be labeled a DC Elseworlds project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:33.198
allowing it to exist in its own world,&nbsp;
far away from the rest of the DC Universe.

00:02:33.198 --> 00:02:38.040
Henry Cavill's Superman might be consigned&nbsp;
to the history books, but that's not going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:43.740
to stop DC from mining as much creative&nbsp;
potential out of Kal-El as they possibly can.

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:48.180
Aside from Gunn's own movie, the studio&nbsp;
is producing an Elseworlds project from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:52.800
Ta-Nehisi Coates. Here's what we know&nbsp;
so far: Coates, known for his powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.940
social journalism and comic book runs&nbsp;
with Black Panther and Captain America,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:02.040
is penning the script. J.J. Abrams and Bad Robot&nbsp;
are attached to the film on the production side,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:06.900
but Abrams isn't in the running to direct.&nbsp;
Instead, DC and Warner Bros. are looking for both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:13.440
a Black director and a Black lead actor for the&nbsp;
film. Sadly, nobody has been confirmed just yet.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.520
As far as the film's plot, The Hollywood&nbsp;
Reporter has claimed that it might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.080
a "20th-century period piece," and&nbsp;
that Coates' version of Superman is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:26.580
"a Kal-El in the vein of the original&nbsp;
Superman comics." Obviously, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:31.740
these are early days, and recent comments&nbsp;
made by Gunn suggested that DC has yet to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:36.031
see a finished script from Coates. For now,&nbsp;
you'll just have to keep your eyes on the sky.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:43.800
Yes, it's finally happening: Kara Zor-El is set&nbsp;
for her big solo cinematic project. Supergirl:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.620
Woman of Tomorrow was another movie announced by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:52.020
Gunn and Safran in January 2023. Based on&nbsp;
the eponymous comic book run by Tom King,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:57.240
Woman of Tomorrow will revolve around a&nbsp;
dark, space-based sci-fi revenge story.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:01.380
"She watched everybody around&nbsp;
her perish in some terrible way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:03.360
so she is a much more jaded character."

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:07.500
King himself has been assisting Gunn in&nbsp;
developing this project, although we're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.360
unsure who will play the darker, harder version&nbsp;
of the character. In the upcoming Flash movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:16.800
Sasha Calle will appear as Supergirl, having&nbsp;
beat out hundreds of others for the role;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:21.420
Gunn and Safran have yet to say whether or not&nbsp;
Calle would reprise the part in Woman of Tomorrow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:25.800
however, and a full reboot and a recast&nbsp;
certainly isn't out of the question.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.940
Expect to hear more about Supergirl's&nbsp;
future in the coming weeks and months.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:36.720
Today, WildStorm is an edgy imprint of DC&nbsp;
Comics, but it began life back in the 20th&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:40.620
century as an independent publisher,&nbsp;
best known for the superhero team-up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:45.540
title Stormwatch. After a while, Stormwatch&nbsp;
morphed into the 1999 spinoff The Authority,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:50.880
which was released after DC absorbed WildStorm&nbsp;
and incorporated its characters into its own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:55.860
narrative canon. In 2023, James Gunn and&nbsp;
Peter Safran announced that a standalone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.860 --> 00:05:01.320
film based on the comic series would be one&nbsp;
of their first priorities as heads of the DCU.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:06.060
Something of a rogue Justice League, the&nbsp;
Authority boasts a revolving membership&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:11.040
including such characters as the electric&nbsp;
Jenny Sparks, the liquid metal-based Engineer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:16.860
the magical Doctor, and the shadowy Midnighter.&nbsp;
During the reveal of the new slate, Gunn said:

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:21.120
"One of the things with the DCU is&nbsp;
it isn't just a story of heroes and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:26.040
villains and not every movie and TV show is&nbsp;
going to be about good guy versus bad guy."

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:31.140
Apparently, that moral gray area will&nbsp;
be where the DCU Authority operates.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:36.300
"There are people that are anti-heroes, and&nbsp;
there are people that are very questionable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:39.720
like the Authority, who basically&nbsp;
believe that you can't fix the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:43.080
in an easy manner, and they sort of&nbsp;
take things into their own hands."

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:48.060
In other words, if the Authority think they can&nbsp;
solve a problem, they'll do it — no matter how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:53.760
violent, controversial, or devastating their&nbsp;
decisions. DC haven't announced a release date&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:58.958
for The Authority yet, but it's due to arrive&nbsp;
in the "Gods &amp; Monsters" chapter of the new DCU.

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:04.380
As heads of the DCU, James Gunn and Peter&nbsp;
Safran are faced with the tricky proposition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:10.080
of balancing multiple Batmans across different&nbsp;
narrative timelines. For example, filmmaker Todd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:14.820
Phillips will continue to tell the story of Dark&nbsp;
Knight adjacent villain the Joker with Joker:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:19.020
Folie à Deux, and Matt Reeves and Robert&nbsp;
Pattinson will release their sequel to The Batman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:24.540
Basically, there's a whole lot of Batmanning&nbsp;
going on in DC's future — but that's not all.

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:29.460
In January 2023, Gunn and Safran&nbsp;
announced yet another Batman project:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:32.640
the official one — the Caped Crusader of record.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:37.740
"Damian Wayne is my favorite Robin,&nbsp;
he's a little assassin who Batman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:41.220
tries to get in line, so this is&nbsp;
the story of the two of them."

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:45.360
Based on Grant Morrison's comics series&nbsp;
of the same name, The Brave and the Bold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:48.360
is part father-son drama, part superhero story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:52.740
and part crime extravaganza. Aside&nbsp;
from Damian Wayne, Safran has said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:56.640
that we can expect to see other members of&nbsp;
Batman's family appear, telling the media:

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:01.128
"We feel like they've been left out of the&nbsp;
Batman stories in the theater for far too long."

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:04.980
Before he was appointed one&nbsp;
of the guardians of the DCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:09.780
and before he brought the Guardians of&nbsp;
Galaxy to the big screen, James Gunn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:14.640
was known for making humor-laced cult horror&nbsp;
movies. Decades later, it looks like Gunn is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:19.260
going back to his roots. As part of the new&nbsp;
slate of DCU projects, Gunn announced that a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:23.940
new Swamp Thing movie was in pre-production as&nbsp;
part of the studio's "Gods &amp; Monsters" chapter.

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:30.120
In the 1980s, the DC Comics character headlined&nbsp;
two campy, low-budget films, and in 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:34.800
a Swamp Thing TV series lasted a&nbsp;
single season. The story concerns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:39.600
kind-hearted botanist Dr. Alec Holland, who&nbsp;
is accidentally transformed into a massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:45.300
green swamp creature and decides to fight bad&nbsp;
guys. Gunn and cohort Peter Safran plan to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:49.800
back to square one with Swamp Thing and&nbsp;
explore the character's "dark origins."

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:53.280
So who will direct? Well,&nbsp;
these are still early days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:58.162
but Deadline has reported that Logan and&nbsp;
Indiana Jones director James Mangold is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.162 --> 00:08:02.220
in talks to helm the upcoming horror movie.&nbsp;
It doesn't have a release date yet either,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:06.876
but horror fans can rest easy knowing that&nbsp;
Swamp Thing is right around the corner.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:12.780
Having gained plenty of superhero experience&nbsp;
during the events of his 2019 solo vehicle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:17.280
young Billy Batson will be ready to&nbsp;
take on some new bad guys in the sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:22.560
Shazam! Fury of the Gods. And he'll have a little&nbsp;
help this time around. At the end of Shazam!,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:27.000
Billy was able to defeat Doctor Sivana by&nbsp;
sharing his powers with his foster family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:32.100
transforming them into Shazam-like heroes who will&nbsp;
have a significant role to play in the sequel.

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:36.900
So who will Billy Batson and his foster&nbsp;
siblings face this time around? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:41.160
it looks like the Daughters of Atlas are&nbsp;
ticked off at the Shazamily for using the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:46.620
power of the gods for their own crime-fighting&nbsp;
purposes. So Oscar-winner Helen Mirren, Lucy Liu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:51.900
and Rachel Zegler are coming to wreak havoc&nbsp;
as Hespera, Kalypso, and Athena. Based on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:56.760
trailers we've seen, it looks like once they get&nbsp;
their hands on a powerful weapon, they'll be able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:02.340
to drain Shazam and his family of their superhero&nbsp;
powers, giving the goddesses a major edge.

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:07.200
Of course, the first Shazam! was a heck of&nbsp;
a lot of fun, but we all know that superhero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:12.360
sequels tend to go darker. It stands to reason,&nbsp;
then, that young Billy is going to have some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:18.471
growing up to do in Shazam! Fury of the Gods.&nbsp;
The sequel is released on March 17th, 2023.

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:25.680
The long-awaited solo film for the Flash has&nbsp;
been cooking since long before his DCEU debut.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:31.020
A long list of writers and directors signed&nbsp;
onto and departed the project over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:36.900
and the movie's progress was only hindered by&nbsp;
Ezra Miller's bizarre crime spree across what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:41.760
seemed like the entire United States.&nbsp;
Nevertheless, the movie is nearly here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:45.720
mostly thanks to the steady hand&nbsp;
of It director Andy Muschietti.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:49.680
The Flash will take its narrative cues&nbsp;
from the iconic "Flashpoint" storyline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:55.620
bringing together various DC properties under&nbsp;
one mind-bogglingly complex multiverse. Expect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.620 --> 00:10:00.480
to see the return of Michael Keaton's Batman&nbsp;
and the debut of Sasha Calle's Supergirl in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:05.580
the new movie — although rumors suggest that&nbsp;
previously filmed appearances from Ben Affleck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:09.900
Gal Gadot, and Jason Momoa may have&nbsp;
been cut from the final product.

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:16.800
"Oh, wow, they really just&nbsp;
vanish, huh? Oh, that's rude."

00:10:18.468 --> 00:10:23.580
Recently, James Gunn has said that The Flash&nbsp;
is one of the greatest superhero movies ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:29.640
made and revealed that it will help reset the&nbsp;
entire DC universe. Interestingly, before Gunn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:34.560
and Peter Safran took over the franchise, it was&nbsp;
reported that DC and Warner were already taking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:39.420
steps toward a sequel. While Gunn has expressed&nbsp;
his desire to work with Muschietti in the future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:44.388
it's currently unknown what role, if any,&nbsp;
Barry Allen will play in the new regime.

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:48.720
The Blue Beetle moniker has been taken up&nbsp;
by a few different characters in the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:54.360
but the upcoming Blue Beetle film will focus&nbsp;
on the most recent: Jaime Reyes. In his comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:58.560
Reyes discovers the Blue Beetle Scarab&nbsp;
entirely by accident and takes it home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:04.080
The artifact swiftly bonds with him and grants him&nbsp;
an extraterrestrial suit of armor and a slew of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:08.760
powers to go with it. He's been part of several&nbsp;
different superhero groups in the DC universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:13.380
so a Blue Beetle film could easily play&nbsp;
into several different IPs, depending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:17.700
on what direction they choose to take the&nbsp;
character — and whether he has a future at all.

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:22.560
Xolo Mariduena will star as the titular superhero&nbsp;
in Blue Beetle, supported by Bruna Marquezine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:27.420
Belissa Escobedo, and Harvey Guillén.&nbsp;
Susan Sarandon will play Victoria Kord,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:32.220
a character created specifically for the&nbsp;
film. Meanwhile, Raoul Max Trujillo [ will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:37.200
be playing Carapax the Indestructible Man,&nbsp;
a villain housed in a mighty robotic body.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:41.580
Gareth Dunnet-Alcocer, who wrote&nbsp;
the 2019 crime thriller Miss Bala,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:45.360
will pen the screenplay for Blue Beetle,&nbsp;
while Angel Manuel Soto will direct,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:52.200
following his work on 2020's Charm City Kings.&nbsp;
Blue Beetle hits theaters on August 18th, 2023.

00:11:52.534 --> 00:11:56.160
Aquaman has been the butt of&nbsp;
pop culture jokes for decades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.160 --> 00:12:00.420
owing to his seemingly lame power set.&nbsp;
Although comic book fans knew better,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:05.640
the zeitgeist simply seemed to have it in for&nbsp;
Arthur Curry and his adventures in Atlantis.

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:09.780
"Did someone say cruise ship on the&nbsp;
ocean? Why didn't you invite me?"

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:11.940
"Oh, to tell the fish to get out&nbsp;
of the way? We figured it out."

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:12.480
"Nice one."

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:17.820
Meanwhile, Jason Momoa's first appearance as&nbsp;
the character in 2017's Justice League was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:23.280
received well, if not rapturously, while the movie&nbsp;
itself underperformed severely at the box office.

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:29.760
But then a funny thing happened: James Wan's&nbsp;
Aquaman, in which Momoa reprised the role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:34.680
became a smash hit, raking in over a&nbsp;
billion dollars worldwide and becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:39.720
the highest-grossing film in the DCEU by a&nbsp;
comfortable margin. It didn't take long for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:44.700
Warner Bros. to determine that they had a hot&nbsp;
property on their hands, and in February 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:50.040
it was confirmed that a sequel was in the works.&nbsp;
Director James Wan will be returning for Aquaman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:55.620
and the Lost Kingdom, as will Momoa and much&nbsp;
of the first movie's principal cast. Aquaman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:59.580
co-screenwriter David Leslie Johnson-McGoldrick&nbsp;
also worked on the script for the sequel.

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:05.400
Interestingly, if one of Wan's Instagram posts is&nbsp;
anything to go by, the "Lost Kingdom" in the title&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:10.860
seems to refer to Necrus. This teleporting,&nbsp;
underwater city has occasionally clashed with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:16.200
Aquaman and the denizens of Atlantis in the&nbsp;
past. Sadly, however, aside from a brief sneak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:21.240
peek at DC Fandome, we've yet to see much more&nbsp;
from Aquaman's second adventure. Even weirder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:26.400
James Gunn recently suggested that The Lost&nbsp;
Kingdom will lead into his Superman movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:31.560
and the new DCU. Was he simply referring&nbsp;
to the chronology of the release slate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:36.300
or did he mean that their stories could be&nbsp;
related? Nobody knows — but we'll find out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:41.734
for sure when the film splashes down&nbsp;
in theaters on December 25th, 2023.

00:13:41.734 --> 00:13:44.460
Rather than adapting a well-known comic storyline,

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:51.060
the 2019 drama Joker was inspired by the long&nbsp;
history of Batman's greatest foe. Director and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:56.820
co-writer Todd Phillips reimagined the character&nbsp;
as Arthur Fleck, a struggling comedian suffering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.820 --> 00:14:02.100
a full-on emotional breakdown. As Joker&nbsp;
earned multiple Academy Award nominations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:07.860
and generated more than $1 billion in ticket&nbsp;
sales, a sequel was always bound to happen.

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:14.280
In fact, mere days after Joker opened to huge&nbsp;
box office numbers, Phillips began discussing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:19.320
the future of DC Comics-based films with Warner&nbsp;
Bros. chairman Toby Emmerich. Rumors of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:24.300
Joker sequel emerged soon after. Details&nbsp;
were thin on the ground until June 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:28.560
when Phillips posted a photo of a script&nbsp;
cover page to his Instagram account,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:33.540
bearing the title Joker: Folie à Deux.&nbsp;
Phillips also snapped a pic of Joaquin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:37.800
Phoenix reading the screenplay, and we can&nbsp;
expect to see the star return to the screen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:42.943
as part two of an Elseworlds series that&nbsp;
will exist outside of the main DC Universe.

00:14:42.943 --> 00:14:44.863
"It's enough to make anyone crazy."

00:14:44.863 --> 00:14:50.880
But Phoenix won't be alone here, as the one&nbsp;
and only Lady Gaga will be making her comic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:56.340
book movie debut as Harley Quinn. Apparently,&nbsp;
she'll get to sing too, as the film is reportedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.340 --> 00:15:01.440
going to be a musical set inside the imposing&nbsp;
Arkham Asylum. And, in case you're wondering,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:06.240
Folie à deux is a form of shared psychosis&nbsp;
in which the delusions and hallucinations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:12.120
experienced by one person are transferred to the&nbsp;
other. Sound familiar? Joker: Folie à Deux began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:18.060
filming on December 10th, 2022; the release&nbsp;
date is currently set as October 4th, 2024.

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:22.800
The idea of a feature film based on the&nbsp;
near-unstoppable alien bounty hunter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:28.380
Lobo has been kicking around before the DCU's&nbsp;
inception, with a Guy Ritchie-directed version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:34.680
discussed as far back as 2009. The project&nbsp;
was revived as part of the DCEU slate in 2016,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:39.840
with San Andreas and Rampage director Brad&nbsp;
Peyton set to helm from a script by Jason Fuchs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:43.680
who previously contributed to the screenplay&nbsp;
for Wonder Woman. It was rumored in early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:48.000
2018 that none other than Michael Bay was&nbsp;
being eyed to take the reins on the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:50.520
and Fuchs was still reported&nbsp;
to be working on the script.

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:54.900
As became a theme with DC, however,&nbsp;
the television side of things quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:59.880
threatened to intervene. The second season&nbsp;
of the Syfy series Krypton saw Irish actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.880 --> 00:16:04.500
Emmett J. Scanlan take on the role of Lobo,&nbsp;
leading some observers to speculate that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:09.480
character's feature film prospects had dimmed. For&nbsp;
a while, there was no official word from Warner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:13.380
leaving fans to wonder whether a starring&nbsp;
vehicle for the ultra-violent baddie was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:19.080
still in the cards. Things got more interesting&nbsp;
in November 2022 when James Gunn teased a possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:24.960
Lobo project in the DCU. Soon after, rumors&nbsp;
began to swirl that Aquaman star and devout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:29.280
Lobo fan Jason Momoa could be interested&nbsp;
in playing the character in the future.

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:34.920
During their DCU reveal, James Gunn and&nbsp;
Peter Safran insisted that Momoa won't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:39.360
be playing two characters at once — but they&nbsp;
didn't shoot down the rumors, either. Safran&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:44.284
said that Momoa has been very clear about how&nbsp;
much he loves Lobo, while Gunn simply said:

00:16:44.284 --> 00:16:46.924
"We'll figure it out after Aquaman 2."

